N:aidlc-workflows
D:Operate awslabs/aidlc-workflows (AI-DLC, MIT-0): install the native aidlc command, configure a project for Claude Code, Kiro, Codex, Cursor, opencode or Copilot, pick a workflow profile, and audit what it pre-approves, hooks and registers, with every write previewed and approved first.
G:aidlc ai-dlc aidlc-workflows workflow-profiles harness approval-gates cli
U[5]:
  Install AI-DLC download-first and verify it instead of piping curl into sh
  Configure one project for one harness with a dry run and a plan token
  Choose a profile such as bugfix express feature or enterprise or the composer
  Audit pre-approved permissions hooks and MCP servers without running aidlc
  Keep MCP host trust Bedrock settings and guard bypasses behind separate approval
S[5]{n,action,details}:
  1,Decide harness profile scope,One harness and one profile; harness ids change between releases so read aidlc config --help
  2,Offline gate,Run scripts/preflight.py with optional --project and --repo; aidlc is never executed
  3,Gate side effects,Separate approval for installer config MCP trust providers bypasses pin update and running a workflow
  4,Follow reference,Install config hooks MCP providers profiles and network branches in references/upstream.md
  5,Verify narrowly,aidlc doctor and config trust --check then a small bugfix or poc on a throwaway branch
R[6]:
  Helper is offline and never proves the runtime works
  README pipes the installer into sh; download first and verify with gh attestation when possible
  Without a compatible gh only SHA-256 protects the install and the release is not code-signed
  --yes never grants MCP consent; defaults start four AWS servers with uvx @latest plus context7
  Host trust and guard bypasses are the user's own acts; never script them silently
  Approval gates belong to the user; never answer one on their behalf
E[2]{desc,in,out}:
  "Install on a server from the README one-liner","User wants curl | sh as root","Explanation that the installer refuses root and a download-then-verify-then-run plan after preflight"
  "Enable every MCP server with --yes","User wants MCP defaults in one command","Dry run plus plan token and an explicit MCP approval question naming context7 and the unpinned uvx servers"
